---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
const title = '2008 Suzuki RM250 — Final-Year Two-Stroke | Marc Sherwood';
const description = '2008 Suzuki RM250 motocross bike in Richmond, BC. Race-built two-stroke with Too-Trick Racing suspension, Magura clutch, Pro Circuit exhaust and extensive extras. Ask for details.';
const photos = [
  {src:'/assets/rm250/rm250-hero.jpg',alt:'2008 Suzuki RM250 in silver graphics, side profile on a stand',caption:'RM250 · Silver graphics'},
  {src:'/assets/rm250/rm250-trailside.jpg',alt:'2008 Suzuki RM250 beside mountain lake after a ride',caption:'Out on the trails'},
  {src:'/assets/rm250/rm250-silver-kit.jpg',alt:'2008 Suzuki RM250 with grey kit and number 42 outdoors',caption:'Side profile'},
  {src:'/assets/rm250/rm250-yellow-kit.jpg',alt:'2008 Suzuki RM250 with yellow and black graphics in garage',caption:'Alternate yellow kit'},
  {src:'/assets/rm250/rm250-pipe-detail.jpg',alt:'Close-up of Suzuki RM250 expansion chamber, frame and bodywork',caption:'Two-stroke details'},
];
const groups = [
 {name:'Suspension, wheels & brakes',parts:['Too-Trick Racing suspension','DID DirtStar ST-X rims and upgraded hubs','Oversized brake rotor and upgraded brakes','Braided brake lines','New tires']},
 {name:'Powertrain & rider controls',parts:['Magura hydraulic clutch','New race clutch','Pro Circuit pipe and silencer','Boyesen RAD Valve','Fastway footpegs','Hammerhead shift lever','ARC folding levers','ProTaper handlebars']},
 {name:'Protection & race details',parts:['Factory-style engine case covers','Pro Circuit temperature indicator stickers on the radiators and cylinder','TM Designworks Slide-N-Guide chain slider and rear guide','Polisport Restyle plastics']},
 {name:'Spares & extras',parts:['Additional plastics and graphics','New-in-box OEM Suzuki spare seat','New-in-box DB tall spare seat','Spare parts and additional equipment — full inventory and photos to follow']}
];
---
<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><BaseHead title={title} description={description} image={{src:'/assets/rm250/rm250-hero.jpg',width:2048,height:1542}}/><meta name="theme-color" content="#101b1d"/><style>
html{scroll-behavior:smooth}body{margin:0;background:#101b1d;color:#f3f4ef;font-family:system-ui,-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',sans-serif}*{box-sizing:border-box}a{color:inherit}.wrap{max-width:1180px;margin:auto;padding:0 24px}header{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:16px;padding:22px 0}header>a{font-weight:850;letter-spacing:-.04em;text-decoration:none}header a b{color:#d8f16a}nav{display:flex;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap;font-size:13px}nav a{text-decoration:none;color:#cfdbd4}nav a:hover{color:#d8f16a}.hero{background:#17282b;position:relative;overflow:hidden}.hero:before{content:'';position:absolute;inset:0;background:linear-gradient(90deg,#101b1dfa 0%,#101b1db9 46%,#101b1d10 100%);z-index:1}.hero-img{position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;object-position:center}.hero-content{position:relative;z-index:2;min-height:620px;display:flex;align-items:center;padding-top:70px;padding-bottom:80px}.hero-content>div{max-width:760px}.eyebrow{color:#d8f16a;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.18em;font-weight:800;font-size:12px}.hero h1{font-size:clamp(70px,12vw,150px);letter-spacing:-.09em;line-height:.86;margin:22px 0 25px;font-weight:900}.hero h1 span{color:#d8f16a}.lead{font-size:clamp(19px,2.6vw,27px);line-height:1.5;max-width:700px;color:#e1e8e0}.tags{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:9px;margin:30px 0}.tags span{font-weight:750;border:1px solid #85978b;padding:10px 14px;font-size:11px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.08em}.btn{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;padding:16px 23px;background:#d8f16a;color:#14221c!important;text-decoration:none;font-size:14px;font-weight:850;border:2px solid #d8f16a}.btn.ghost{background:transparent;color:#d8f16a!important}.actions{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:12px}.section{padding:86px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #354946}.section.alt{background:#142327}.section h2{font-size:clamp(36px,5vw,62px);letter-spacing:-.06em;line-height:1.09;margin:13px 0 27px}.copy{max-width:830px;font-size:18px;line-height:1.78;color:#d1dbd5}.copy p{margin:0 0 20px}.gallery{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(12,minmax(0,1fr));gap:13px;margin-top:35px}.photo{grid-column:span 4;display:block;position:relative;background:#1c2e30;overflow:hidden;aspect-ratio:4/3}.photo:nth-child(1),.photo:nth-child(2){grid-column:span 6}.photo img{width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;display:block;transition:transform .2s}.photo:hover img{transform:scale(1.025)}.photo span{position:absolute;bottom:0;left:0;right:0;padding:24px 14px 12px;font-size:13px;font-weight:650;background:linear-gradient(transparent,#101b1dcf)}.cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:15px;margin-top:37px}.card{padding:28px;border:1px solid #3d5550;background:#1b3030}.card h3{font-size:22px;letter-spacing:-.04em;margin:0 0 16px}.card ul{padding-left:20px;color:#d1ddd5;line-height:1.8;font-size:15px}.note{color:#aabeb4;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;margin-top:18px}.companion{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:45px;align-items:center}.companion img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto}.companion h2{margin-top:12px}.contact{background:#d8f16a;color:#142219;padding:80px 0}.contact .eyebrow{color:#5a6f2b}.contact h2{font-size:clamp(42px,6vw,75px);line-height:1;letter-spacing:-.06em;margin:14px 0 28px}.contact p{font-size:18px;max-width:700px;line-height:1.65}.contact .btn{background:#172923;border-color:#172923;color:#d8f16a!important;margin-top:12px}footer{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:15px;color:#a9bbb1;padding:28px 0;font-size:12px}a:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #d8f16a;outline-offset:4px}@media(max-width:760px){.hero-content{min-height:600px}.hero:before{background:linear-gradient(#101b1d9c,#101b1de8)}.section{padding:62px 0}.photo,.photo:nth-child(1),.photo:nth-child(2){grid-column:span 6}.cards,.companion{grid-template-columns:1fr}.companion{gap:24px}}@media(max-width:490px){.photo,.photo:nth-child(1),.photo:nth-child(2){grid-column:span 12}.hero h1{font-size:clamp(66px,19vw,110px)}}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){html{scroll-behavior:auto}.photo img{transition:none}}
.valuehero{display:grid;grid-template-columns:2fr 1fr;gap:18px;padding:30px;background:#101b1d;border:1px solid #49615a;margin:35px 0 24px}.valuehero strong{display:block;color:#d8f16a;font-size:clamp(38px,6vw,78px);line-height:1.12;letter-spacing:-.06em;margin-top:12px}.valuehero p{margin:12px 0 0;color:#cfdbd4;line-height:1.6}.valueaside{border-left:1px solid #49615a;padding-left:24px}.valueaside h3,.unpriced h3{font-size:25px;margin:6px 0}.valuekey{display:flex;gap:22px;flex-wrap:wrap;color:#c3d1c9;font-size:13px;margin:10px 0}.valuekey i{display:inline-block;width:14px;height:14px;background:#d8f16a;vertical-align:middle;margin-right:5px}.valuekey span+span i{background:#719d8b}.valuetable{overflow-x:auto}.valuetable table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;min-width:660px;background:#182a2b}.valuetable th,.valuetable td{text-align:left;padding:16px;border-bottom:1px solid #49615a;vertical-align:middle}.valuetable tbody th{width:36%}.valuetable td{color:#c3d1c9;line-height:1.5}.valuetable .amount,.valuetable .total td:nth-child(2){font-weight:800;color:#d8f16a;white-space:nowrap}.mod-meter{display:flex;height:9px;background:#324642;margin-top:10px}.mod-meter span{background:#d8f16a}.mod-meter i{background:#719d8b}.valuetable .total{background:#101b1d;font-size:18px}.unpriced{border-left:4px solid #d8f16a;padding:12px 22px;margin-top:28px}@media(max-width:760px){.valuehero{grid-template-columns:1fr;padding:22px}.valueaside{border-left:0;border-top:1px solid #49615a;padding:18px 0 0}}</style></head><body><header class="wrap"><a href="/">Marc Sherwood<b>.</b></a><nav aria-label="Page navigation"><a href="#photos">Photos</a><a href="#build">The build</a><a href="#value">Build value</a><a href="#rm125">RM125</a><a href="#contact">Inquire</a></nav></header><main>
<section class="hero"><img class="hero-img" src="/assets/rm250/rm250-hero.jpg" alt="2008 Suzuki RM250 with grey graphics and number 42" fetchpriority="high"/><div class="wrap hero-content"><div><div class="eyebrow">Richmond, BC · Final-year two-stroke</div><h1>2008<br/><span>RM250.</span></h1><p class="lead">A proper, race-prepared Suzuki two-stroke. Too-Trick Racing suspension, Magura hydraulic clutch, Pro Circuit exhaust and a whole lot of character.</p><div class="tags"><span>250cc two-stroke</span><span>2008 · final year</span><span>Ex-racer build</span><span>$5.4k–$7.1k+ selected mods</span></div><div class="actions"><a class="btn" href="#contact">Ask about the bike ↗</a><a class="btn ghost" href="#photos">View photos ↓</a><a class="btn ghost" href="#value">Explore the build value ↓</a></div></div></div></section>
<section class="section" id="photos"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">01 / Photo gallery</div><h2>See it from every angle.</h2><p class="copy">Photos of the actual RM250, shown in more than one set of plastics. Click any photo to open the full-size version.</p><div class="gallery">{photos.map(photo=><a class="photo" href={photo.src} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><img src={photo.src} alt={photo.alt} loading="lazy" decoding="async"/><span>{photo.caption} ↗</span></a>)}</div></div></section>
<section class="section alt" id="story"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">02 / The story</div><h2>Not just another old dirt bike.</h2><div class="copy"><p>This is a <strong>2008 Suzuki RM250</strong>, the final production year of Suzuki's 250cc two-stroke motocross machine. It's an ex-racer with the kind of equipment and attention that makes it stand out from a stock bike.</p><p>I'm making room for a purpose-built enduro for BC singletrack. The RM250 deserves a rider who will appreciate everything that has gone into it.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="section" id="build"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">03 / The build</div><h2>The good stuff.</h2><div class="cards">{groups.map(group=><article class="card"><h3>{group.name}</h3><ul>{group.parts.map(part=><li>{part}</li>)}</ul></article>)}</div><p class="note">Exact component variants and detailed internal engine specification can be confirmed when reviewing the bike. Parts shown across photos may vary with the installed graphics or equipment.</p></div></section>
<section class="section alt" id="value"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">04 / Replacement cost of the upgrades</div><h2>This is not a cheap build.</h2><p class="copy">A lot of the investment is where it counts: wheels and suspension, power delivery, braking, and rider control. These are not just cosmetic add-ons. Here's what the selected aftermarket equipment would roughly cost to replace with comparable new parts.</p><div class="valuehero"><div><span class="eyebrow">Selected upgrades alone</span><strong>$5,436–$7,085+</strong><p>CAD · estimated new replacement parts · before tax</p></div><div class="valueaside"><h3>11 line items</h3><p>Not including the motorcycle, installation labour, or other equipment and spares listed below.</p></div></div><div class="valuekey"><span><i></i> Low estimate</span><span><i></i> Additional range</span></div><div class="valuetable"><table><thead><tr><th>Modification</th><th>Estimated CAD</th><th>Basis / notes</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row"><span>DID DirtStar ST-X rims & hubs</span><div class="mod-meter" aria-hidden="true"><span style="width:62.06896551724138%"></span><i style="width:37.93103448275862%"></i></div></th><td class="amount">$1,800–$2,900+</td><td>Complete billet-hub wheelsets; cost depends on hub and wheel specification.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><span>Too-Trick Racing suspension</span><div class="mod-meter" aria-hidden="true"><span style="width:29.310344827586203%"></span><i style="width:0%"></i></div></th><td class="amount">$850+</td><td>Budget baseline for revalving; exact services and parts can increase cost.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><span>Pro Circuit full exhaust</span><div class="mod-meter" aria-hidden="true"><span style="width:25.379310344827587%"></span><i style="width:7.03448275862069%"></i></div></th><td class="amount">$736–$940</td><td>Works pipe and R304 silencer.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><span>Oversized rotor & braided line</span><div class="mod-meter" aria-hidden="true"><span style="width:16.724137931034484%"></span><i style="width:0.5517241379310345%"></i></div></th><td class="amount">$485–$501</td><td>270 mm floating rotor kit and braided brake line.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><span>Fastway footpegs & fit kit</span><div class="mod-meter" aria-hidden="true"><span style="width:10.86206896551724%"></span><i style="width:4%"></i></div></th><td class="amount">$315–$431</td><td>Steel or aluminum Evolution variants.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><span>Boyesen RAD Valve</span><div class="mod-meter" aria-hidden="true"><span style="width:8.827586206896552%"></span><i style="width:1.3103448275862069%"></i></div></th><td class="amount">$256–$294</td><td>Model-specific reed intake.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><span>Polisport Restyle plastics</span><div class="mod-meter" aria-hidden="true"><span style="width:9.96551724137931%"></span><i style="width:0%"></i></div></th><td class="amount">$289</td><td>Complete restyle kit for the 2001–2008 RM250.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><span>TM Designworks Slide-N-Guide</span><div class="mod-meter" aria-hidden="true"><span style="width:9.827586206896552%"></span><i style="width:0%"></i></div></th><td class="amount">$285</td><td>Chain slider and rear guide kit.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><span>ARC folding levers (pair)</span><div class="mod-meter" aria-hidden="true"><span style="width:7.551724137931035%"></span><i style="width:3.7586206896551726%"></i></div></th><td class="amount">$219–$328</td><td>Two folding levers or perch assemblies.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><span>ProTaper handlebars</span><div class="mod-meter" aria-hidden="true"><span style="width:4.620689655172414%"></span><i style="width:1.8275862068965518%"></i></div></th><td class="amount">$134–$187</td><td>Contour 1-1/8 inch bars.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><span>Hammerhead shift lever</span><div class="mod-meter" aria-hidden="true"><span style="width:2.310344827586207%"></span><i style="width:0.44827586206896547%"></i></div></th><td class="amount">$67–$80</td><td>Forged aluminum shifter.</td></tr><tr class="total"><th scope="row">Selected parts total</th><td>$5,436–$7,085+</td><td>Before tax and labour</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class="note">Owner-provided approximate replacement-cost estimates. Exact variants, suppliers, availability, exchange rates and suspension work may change costs. The suspension estimate is a starting point, not a ceiling. These figures are not a resale appraisal or the asking price. Detailed component identification can be confirmed at viewing.</p><div class="unpriced"><h3>And that isn't everything.</h3><p class="copy">The Magura hydraulic clutch, new race clutch, new tires, factory-style case covers, Pro Circuit temperature indicators, alternate plastics and graphics, both new-in-box seats, and additional spares are not included in this priced total. The bike is a complete package, not a pile of parts to buy and fit.</p></div></div></section><section class="section alt" id="rm125"><div class="wrap companion"><div><div class="eyebrow">05 / The little sister</div><h2>There's an RM125, too.</h2><div class="copy"><p>The bike with the <strong>red-and-black seat</strong> is not the RM250. Meet <strong>Suzanne</strong>, a separate <strong>2007 Suzuki RM125</strong> that received a frame-up rebuild.</p><p>It could potentially be rehomed alongside the RM250. <a href="/rm125/" style="color:#d8f16a;font-weight:700">See Suzanne’s rebuild story →</a></p></div></div><a href="/assets/rm250/rm125-companion.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><img src="/assets/rm250/rm125-companion.jpg" alt="2007 Suzuki RM125 with red and black seat and yellow bodywork, separately available companion bike" loading="lazy"/></a></div></section>
<section class="contact" id="contact"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">06 / Inquire</div><h2>Interested in the RM?</h2><p>Located in Richmond, British Columbia. Get in touch to discuss the build, included extras, viewing arrangements or the possibility of taking both Suzukis home.</p><a class="btn" href="mailto:marcsherwood@gmail.com?subject=2008%20Suzuki%20RM250%20Inquiry">Email about the RM250 ↗</a></div></section></main><footer class="wrap"><span>© Marc Sherwood · Richmond, BC</span><a href="/">Back to marcsherwood.com</a></footer></body></html>
